    "connector.eyebrow": "AI AGENTS", "connector.title": "AI connector", "connector.offIntro": "Let an AI agent on this computer (Claude Code, Codex, Claude Desktop) check and import prototypes, run builds and previews, export .xbsite files and, if you choose, send to WordPress in development. It can never publish, deploy, read credentials or settings, or delete anything in Publish; on WordPress, removals always wait for your confirmation.", "connector.enable": "Turn on the connector", "connector.autoStart": "Turn it back on when Histeon Publish starts", "connector.enabledNotice": "Connector on: connect your agent with one of the commands below.", "connector.stoppedNotice": "Connector off: agents can no longer use it.", "connector.stop": "Stop", "connector.interrupt": "Interrupt", "connector.interrupted": "Operation interrupted.", "connector.nothingRunning": "Nothing was running.", "connector.since": "On since {time}", "connector.lastAgent": "last agent: {name} (self-reported)", "connector.noAgent": "no agent yet", "connector.runningNow": "Running: {operation} · {client}", "connector.unavailable": "Cannot read the connector status.", "connector.retry": "Try again",
    "connector.connectTitle": "Connect your agent", "connector.tab.claudeCode": "Claude Code", "connector.tab.codex": "Codex", "connector.tab.claudeDesktop": "Claude Desktop", "connector.tab.chatgptDesktop": "ChatGPT desktop", "connector.tab.generic": "Other MCP client", "connector.tab.cli": "Command line", "connector.hint.claudeCode": "Paste it in a terminal: it adds Histeon Publish as an MCP server for your user.", "connector.hint.codex": "Paste it in a terminal.", "connector.hint.codexToml": "Or add this block to ~/.codex/config.toml: it gives long builds 180 seconds.", "connector.hint.claudeDesktop": "In Claude Desktop open Settings → Developer → Edit Config, add this block to claude_desktop_config.json and restart Claude Desktop.", "connector.hint.chatgptDesktop": "Or by hand: in the ChatGPT desktop app open Settings → MCP servers → Add server, choose STDIO, name it histos-publish and paste this command (if the form has separate command and arguments: the first part is the command, the rest the arguments). Save and restart the server.", "connector.hint.chatgptChat": "The easiest way: paste this message in the ChatGPT desktop chat. If ChatGPT can run commands on this computer it connects by itself; if it cannot add MCP servers, it uses Histeon Publish from the command line. If it cannot run commands at all, use the form below.", "connector.chatMessage": "Connect to Histeon Publish, which is open on this computer with the AI connector on. The command holds no secrets.\n\n1. Add this MCP server to your configuration, in ~/.codex/config.toml (create the file if it is missing and keep what it already holds), then reload the MCP servers:\n\n{toml}\n\nCheck with /mcp that histos-publish is connected and use its hp_* tools: hp_status first, then hp_manual.\n\n2. If you cannot add MCP servers, use the command line, which has the same operations:\n\n{cli}\n\nlists the commands (status, check, import, build, manual…): use them in place of help. Start with status, then manual.\n\nTell me which way you used and what status answers.", "connector.hint.chatgptToml": "Or add this block to ~/.codex/config.toml: the ChatGPT desktop app, Codex CLI and the IDE extension read the same configuration, so if Codex is already connected there is nothing else to do.", "connector.hint.generic": "For any MCP client that starts stdio servers: this is the command to run.", "connector.hint.cli": "For agents without MCP: the script lists the available commands.", "connector.noSecrets": "The command contains no secrets.", "connector.copy": "Copy", "connector.copied": "Copied to the clipboard.", "connector.copyFailed": "Copy failed: select the text and copy it by hand.", "connector.firstMessage": "Suggested first message", "connector.firstMessageText": "Check ~/proposals/site.html and import it into Histeon Publish", "connector.remoteImages": "The agent downloads a prototype’s remote images only when it asks for that explicitly.", "connector.guideDone": "Connected", "connector.guideTodo": "To do", "connector.step.node": "Node.js on this computer", "connector.node.searching": "Looking for Node.js…", "connector.node.found": "Node.js {version} found: the commands below use {path}.", "connector.node.old": "Node.js {version} is too old: version 18 or later is needed. Update it from nodejs.org; this screen notices by itself.", "connector.node.missing": "Node.js not found. Install it from nodejs.org (version 18 or later): the agent needs it to start the connection. This screen notices by itself.", "connector.step.command": "Add Histeon Publish to your agent", "connector.step.agent": "Restart the agent and wait for it to show up", "connector.agent.waiting": "Waiting for your agent… After adding the command, restart the agent and ask it something about Histeon Publish.", "connector.agent.connected": "{name} is connected.", "connector.agent.before": "An agent connected before: when you use it again it shows up here.", "connector.askTitle": "Ask your agent", "connector.askHint": "Name the prototype to import and paste the message in the agent’s chat.", "connector.prototypePath": "Prototype path", "connector.prototypePathPlaceholder": "/path/to/prototype.html", "connector.choosePrototype": "Choose the prototype file", "connector.chooseFailed": "Cannot open the file chooser: type the path by hand.", "connector.firstMessageFor": "Check \"{path}\" and import it into Histeon Publish",
