    "cms.conversionFramework": "Target framework", "cms.conversionFramework.histos-css": "Histeon CSS (recommended, free)", "cms.conversionFramework.acss": "Automatic.css (only if active on the WordPress site)", "cms.conversionFramework.core": "Core Framework (free, default preset)", "cms.conversionFrameworkHint.core": "Spaces and text sizes become Core Framework variables (--space-m, --text-l…) when they match the default preset's scale within a twentieth (at 1280 px). The variables used are defined in a sheet of the project; on WordPress with Core active, Core's own apply. Colors and fonts stay as they are.", "cms.conversionFramework.none": "None: values as they are", "cms.conversionFrameworkHint.histos-css": "Colors, fonts, text sizes and spaces become Histeon CSS tokens when they match the scale within a twentieth (at 1280 px); the others stay numbers. Changing the framework converts the site again.", "cms.conversionFrameworkHint.acss": "The same values become Automatic.css variables (--space-m, --text-l, --primary…). ACSS is paid and not included: in Publish the values come from the linked Histeon CSS tokens.", "cms.conversionFrameworkHint.none": "The CSS keeps the site's values, without a framework's variables.", "cms.conversionReportDownload": "Download the conversion report (JSON)", "cms.conversionExact": "Exact values: keep the hand-written sizes as the site’s variables", "cms.conversionExactHint": "Text and spacing sizes written in px or rem stay as they were, as Site variables (Design), instead of moving to the nearest step of the framework’s scale. The site then looks like the original at every width; colors and fonts go to the tokens as always. Unchecked, the conversion is the usual one.", "cms.conversionExactHint.always": "A captured proposal always keeps its exact sizes, as Site variables (Design): it is what the client approved.", "cms.conversionRecipes": "Without JavaScript: use the recipes instead of the site’s scripts", "cms.conversionRecipesHint": "Menus, accordions, tabs, carousels and modals become HTML and CSS that also work in the builder; the site’s scripts are not kept. Uncheck to keep them.", "cms.reportHistory": "Import reports kept in the project ({n})", "cms.reportDownload": "Download as JSON", "cms.conversionDesign": "Proposal for Histeon CSS, from the site’s colors and fonts:", "cms.conversionTokensOn": "Converted with Histeon CSS tokens and this design:", "cms.conversionAcssOn": "Converted with Automatic.css variables and this design:", "cms.conversionDesignHint": "With a framework the site uses these colors and fonts as the project’s design, which you then change. The scale is fluid: sizes change a little across screens, check the preview before importing.", "cms.design.primary": "Primary color", "cms.design.secondary": "Secondary color", "cms.design.font_body": "Text", "cms.design.font_heading": "Headings",
